// tests/ll_cs_vectors_tests.nv — the plan of a Channel Sounding procedure against the sample data of [Vol 6] Part C, Section 8.1
// (Channel Selection Algorithm #3b): four sets, each a configuration and the steps of the procedure it gives, from the access addresses
// and channels to the sequences, tone extension slots and antenna path permutation of every step.
//
// Sets 1 to 3 give each step's draws and the shuffled channel lists; their subevents close after a number of steps the sample does not
// derive (it asks for "at least 20 steps"), so each row of `S*_SUBS` names the steps of a subevent and the test closes the subevent
// there.  Set 4 comes with the scheduling of the procedure (subevents of 4 ms every 5 ms, T_PM 10 microseconds, T_SW 10 microseconds, LE 2M,
// a 96-bit sounding sequence), so its subevents close where the step times say: 6 steps each.  The sets share one key, the values of
// [Vol 6] Part C, Section 7.
//
// The numbers below are those of the sample data, one row for each step: the step number, its mode, whether it repeats a step of the
// subevent before (1) or not (0), the channel, the nanoseconds from the start of the subevent to the first packet or tone (-1 where the
// sample gives none), the access addresses of the initiator and of the reflector (-1 for a step with no CS_SYNC), the tone extension slot of
// each (-1 for a step with no tones), the antenna path permutation index (-1 for none), and the sounding sequence of the initiator and of
// the reflector as four 32-bit words each (the first word holds the first 32 bits sent, the first of them in bit 0).  The channels of
// sets 1 to 3 follow from the shuffled lists of the sample and the rules of [Vol 6] Part H, Section 4.2; those of set 4 are the ones
// it prints.  `tests/cs_vectors.py` writes the numbers from the text of the specification.
//
//   novo test tests/ll_cs_vectors_tests.nv

